{
  "id": "fluency-l3-second-partials",
  "lesson": "l3-second-partials",
  "title": "Fluency: second partial derivatives",
  "n": 20,
  "pass": 0.9,
  "minutes": 10,
  "families": [
    {
      "id": "first-partial",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "find a first partial derivative",
      "vars": {
        "c": { "int": [-4, 4], "not": [0] },
        "m": { "int": [2, 4] },
        "n": { "int": [3, 5] },
        "b": { "int": [-5, 5], "not": [0] },
        "p": { "int": [3, 5] },
        "e": { "int": [-5, 5], "not": [0] },
        "q": { "int": [3, 5] }
      },
      "let": {
        "cn": "c*n",
        "bp": "b*p",
        "eq": "e*q"
      },
      "where": ["n != q"],
      "prompt": "Take $f(x, y) = {c:c}x^{{{m}}}y^{{{n}}}{b:+c}x^{{{p}}}{e:+c}y^{{{q}}}$. Find $f_y$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "{cn}x^{{{m}}}y^{{{n-1}}}{eq:+}y^{{{q-1}}}", "keyboard": "calculus", "label": "f sub y" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "x-term-differentiated", "tex": "{cn}x^{{{m}}}y^{{{n-1}}}{bp:+}x^{{{p-1}}}{eq:+}y^{{{q-1}}}", "line": "You differentiated ${b:c}x^{{{p}}}$. With $x$ held fixed it is a constant, so its $y$-derivative is 0." },
        { "id": "x-factor-dropped", "tex": "{cn}y^{{{n-1}}}{eq:+}y^{{{q-1}}}", "line": "You dropped $x^{{{m}}}$. A held $x$ is a constant factor, so it stays in front." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Hold $x$ fixed: $x^{{{m}}}$ is a constant factor and ${b:c}x^{{{p}}}$ is a constant, with $y$-derivative 0.",
        "Differentiate the powers of $y$: $f_y = {cn}x^{{{m}}}y^{{{n-1}}}{eq:+}y^{{{q-1}}}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bend-at-a-point",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "evaluate a second partial at a point",
      "vars": {
        "c": { "int": [-2, 2], "not": [0] },
        "n": { "int": [2, 3] },
        "b": { "int": [-2, 2], "not": [0] },
        "e": { "int": [-5, 5], "not": [0] },
        "q": { "int": [2, 4] },
        "x0": { "int": [-2, 2], "not": [0] },
        "y0": { "int": [-2, 2], "not": [0] }
      },
      "let": {
        "c3": "3*c",
        "b4": "4*b",
        "c6": "6*c",
        "b12": "12*b",
        "t1": "6*c*x0*y0^n",
        "t2": "12*b*x0^2",
        "key": "6*c*x0*y0^n + 12*b*x0^2",
        "fx": "3*c*x0^2*y0^n + 4*b*x0^3",
        "fxy": "3*c*n*x0^2*y0^(n-1)"
      },
      "where": ["key != fx", "key != fxy", "fx != fxy"],
      "prompt": "Take $f(x, y) = {c:c}x^3y^{{{n}}}{b:+c}x^4{e:+c}y^{{{q}}}$. What is $f_{{xx}}$ at $({x0}, {y0})$?",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{key}", "tol": { "abs": 0 }, "placeholder": "For example 24" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "stopped-at-first", "value": "{fx}", "line": "That is $f_x$ at the point. Differentiate in $x$ once more to get $f_{{xx}}$." },
        { "id": "mixed-instead", "value": "{fxy}", "line": "That is $f_{{xy}}$: you differentiated in $y$ the second time. $f_{{xx}}$ uses $x$ both times." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "$f_x = {c3}x^2y^{{{n}}}{b4:+}x^3$, since ${e:c}y^{{{q}}}$ is a constant in $x$.",
        "$f_{{xx}} = {c6}xy^{{{n}}}{b12:+}x^2$.",
        "At $({x0}, {y0})$ the two terms are ${t1}$ and ${t2}$, so $f_{{xx}} = {key}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "mixed-partial",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "find a mixed partial derivative",
      "vars": {
        "c": { "int": [-4, 4], "not": [0] },
        "m": { "int": [3, 4] },
        "n": { "int": [3, 4] },
        "b": { "int": [-5, 5], "not": [0] },
        "p": { "int": [3, 5] },
        "e": { "int": [-5, 5], "not": [0] },
        "q": { "int": [3, 5] }
      },
      "let": {
        "cm": "c*m",
        "cn": "c*n",
        "bp": "b*p",
        "eq": "e*q",
        "cmn": "c*m*n"
      },
      "prompt": "Take $f(x, y) = {c:c}x^{{{m}}}y^{{{n}}}{b:+c}x^{{{p}}}{e:+c}y^{{{q}}}$. Find the mixed partial $f_{{xy}}$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "{cmn}x^{{{m-1}}}y^{{{n-1}}}", "keyboard": "calculus", "label": "f sub x y" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "product-of-partials", "tex": "({cm}x^{{{m-1}}}y^{{{n}}}{bp:+}x^{{{p-1}}})({cn}x^{{{m}}}y^{{{n-1}}}{eq:+}y^{{{q-1}}})", "line": "That is $f_x \\times f_y$. The mixed partial differentiates $f_x$ again, in $y$." },
        { "id": "pure-term-kept", "tex": "{cmn}x^{{{m-1}}}y^{{{n-1}}}{bp:+}x^{{{p-1}}}", "line": "You kept ${bp}x^{{{p-1}}}$ from $f_x$. It has no $y$, so its $y$-derivative is 0." },
        { "id": "power-not-lowered", "tex": "{cmn}x^{{{m-1}}}y^{{{n}}}", "line": "You brought the power of $y$ down but did not lower it by one." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "$f_x = {cm}x^{{{m-1}}}y^{{{n}}}{bp:+}x^{{{p-1}}}$.",
        "Differentiate in $y$: the second term has no $y$, so $f_{{xy}} = {cmn}x^{{{m-1}}}y^{{{n-1}}}$."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
